WimpLib
=======

A library of JavaScript modules shared by the desktop's programs:
reading and writing zip files and XML, text measuring, number,
font and colour lists, and the parts of a toolbar and a ruler. Word
($.MoreApps.!Word) uses it to open, show and save .docx files, and
your own programs can use it too. It is not a program:
double-clicking it shows this text.

Where it is
-----------
It lives in $.!Boot.Resources.!WimpLib, with the other system
resources. At start-up the desktop runs its !Boot file, which sets
two system variables (*Show WimpLib$* lists them):

  WimpLib$Dir      the library's directory
  WimpLib$Path     where programs look for its modules: a list of
                   directories, each ending in '.', with commas
                   between them (normally just <WimpLib$Dir>.)

and WimpLib$Version. A variable that is already set is kept.

Using it in a program
---------------------
A JavaScript program (file type JSScript) imports a module by its
name after 'wimplib/', wherever the program is:

  import { readZip, writeZip } from 'wimplib/Zip';
  import { parseXml, serialize } from 'wimplib/Xml';

The name is looked for in each directory of WimpLib$Path in turn
(as Name, then Name/js); the first one found is used. If it is in
none of them, WimpLib$Dir is tried last. 'wimplib' may be in any
case; a module name is letters, digits, _ and -, with / between
directories, so an import cannot reach outside the library.

From the command line or an Obey file the files are, for example,
<WimpLib$Dir>.Zip, or WimpLib:Zip.

Using your own copy
-------------------
To try a changed module without touching this one, put it in a
directory of your own and add that directory to the front of the
path, after the desktop has started (it runs no boot file of yours
before this library's !Boot):

  Set WimpLib$Path RAM::RamDisc0.$.MyLib.,<WimpLib$Dir>.

Programs started after that find your module first. Copy a module
with the files it imports (Zip needs ZipRead, ZipWrite and
ZipError): the library's modules import each other by relative
names, so a changed inner module is not seen by the others that
import it. WimpLib$Path is stored with <WimpLib$Dir> filled in, so
changing WimpLib$Dir later has no effect until WimpLib$Path is
set again.

The modules
-----------
  Zip        readZip and writeZip: zip files (and so .docx files)
  ZipRead    reading the entries of a zip file (used by Zip)
  ZipWrite   building a zip file (used by Zip)
  ZipNames   which entry names are safe to unpack (used by Zip)
  ZipError   the error a damaged or unusable zip file gives
  Crc32      the CRC-32 checksum of zip files, PNG and gzip
  Xml        parseXml and serialize: a small, safe XML parser and
             writer that keeps a document exactly as it was
  XmlParse   the parser (used by Xml)
  XmlWrite   the writer, and helpers for XML trees (used by Xml)
  XmlText    escaping and character checks (used by Xml)
  Segment    grapheme and word boundaries in text
  TextMetrics  text widths and hit testing, measured once
  FontList   font names for a menu: a document's, Word's, the
             desktop's, each once
  NumberField  reading and writing a number field ('11.5' points)
  ColourList the colours of the colour popup; hex colours
  RulerMath  a ruler's inches, ticks and snapping; indent markers

and, in the directory Ui, parts of a program's windows:

  Ui.Toolbar     a row of buttons across the top of a window (a
                 pane): toggles, radio groups, popup arrows, fields
  Ui.ColourPopup a box of colour swatches, opened as a menu
  Ui.FontMenu    a menu of font names
  Ui.Ruler       a ruler in inches under a toolbar, with markers to
                 drag
  Ui.RulerPaint  draws a Ui.Ruler (used by Ui.Ruler)
  Ui.PaneWheel   sends the wheel over a pane to its window (used by
                 Ui.Toolbar and Ui.Ruler)
  Ui.SaveQuery   the Save / Discard / Cancel box asked before
                 changes are thrown away
  Ui.FindBox     a Find and Replace box (fields, Match case, Whole
                 words, Find next...); the program does the finding

A module in Ui is imported as, for example, 'wimplib/Ui/Toolbar'.
The modules outside Ui work anywhere; Ui.Toolbar, Ui.ColourPopup,
Ui.FontMenu, Ui.Ruler, Ui.SaveQuery and Ui.FindBox need the desktop
(they make windows, panes and menus).

Each one says at its top what it offers: load it into !Edit.

The guide $.Docs.Word says more, in its part for programmers.
